{{#is_alert}}backend-worker sent no worker.heartbeat span in 30 minutes. Either the worker is down, its outbox poll loop is hung or cannot reach the database, or the Datadog agent's OTLP receiver is down. No telemetry is not healthy.{{/is_alert}}
{{#is_recovery}}backend-worker heartbeats are arriving again.{{/is_recovery}}

The worker's metrics listener binds 127.0.0.1 and is not scraped, so this monitor uses a trace signal. Since RT-684 the outbox drainer's idle poll is untraced; after each successful poll it records a force-sampled worker.heartbeat root span at most every 5 minutes, so a healthy worker sends about 6 in 30 minutes however long it has been idle. default_zero evaluates missing data as 0, so missing heartbeats raise this alert; there is no separate no-data state.
